## 📍 DAY 1 – LOWER MANHATTAN & BROOKLYN  
**Theme:** Skyline, history, and waterfront views.  

| Time (approx.) | Attraction | What to Do / Highlights | Opening Hours* | Ticket (Adult) | Suggested Visit |
|----------------|------------|--------------------------|----------------|----------------|-----------------|
| **08:30 – 09:30** | **Statue of Liberty & Ellis Island** | • Ferry from Battery Park (reserve a pedestal ticket). <br>• Walk the pedestal for close‑up views. <br>• Explore the Ellis Island Immigration Museum. | 08:30 – 16:00 (last ferry 15:00) | $24.99 (ferry + pedestal) | 1 hr (round‑trip) |
| **10:30 – 12:00** | **One World Observatory** | • 102‑floor “SkyPod” with interactive digital sky‑maps. <br>• Photo‑ops of the Freedom Tower and Manhattan. | 09:00 – 21:00 (last entry 20:00) | $38 (standard) | 1 hr 30 min (incl. security) |
| **12:30 – 13:30** | **Lunch – Financial District** (e.g., Leo’s Bagels, Stone Street) | Grab a quick sandwich or a classic New York pizza slice. | — | — | 1 hr |
| **14:00 – 15:30** | **Brooklyn Bridge Walk** | • Walk the historic pedestrian walkway (≈1.3 mi). <br>• Stop at the **Brooklyn Bridge Park** promenade for skyline photos. | Open 24 h | Free (audio guide $12 optional) | 1 hr 30 min |
| **16:00 – 18:00** | **DUMBO & Brooklyn Bridge Park** | • Iconic photo spot at Washington St & Water St (Manhattan Bridge framing). <br>• Visit **Jane’s Carousel** (small fee). <br>• Grab a coffee at **Almondine Bakery**. | 06:00 – 22:00 (park) | Free (carousel $5) | 2 hr |
| **Evening** | **Dinner in Brooklyn** (e.g., Juliana’s Pizza, The River Café) | Enjoy waterfront dining with Manhattan views. | — | — | — |

### Why this route works
- **Geography:** All stops sit within a 2‑mile stretch, so you can walk or take a short subway ride (4/5 lines).  
- **Flow:** Starts with a classic “must‑see” (Statue), moves to a modern sky‑deck (One World), then finishes with a scenic bridge walk and relaxed Brooklyn vibe.  
- **Timing:** Gives enough buffer for security lines at the Observatory and ferry schedules for the Statue.

---

## 📍 DAY 2 – MIDTOWN & UPPER‑MANHATTAN  
**Theme:** Culture, iconic skyscrapers, and green space.  

| Time (approx.) | Attraction | What to Do / Highlights | Opening Hours* | Ticket (Adult) | Suggested Visit |
|----------------|------------|--------------------------|----------------|----------------|-----------------|
| **08:30 – 09:30** | **Times Square** | • Walk the neon‑lit plaza, snap photos at the red steps. <br>• Optional quick stop at **Madame Tussauds** (separate fee). | Open 24 h | Free (shows/attractions extra) | 1 hr |
| **10:00 – 11:30** | **Empire State Building – 86th‑Floor Observatory** | • Art‑Deco lobby tour. <br>• 360° view from the 86th floor (optional 102‑floor upgrade). | 08:00 – 02:00 (last entry 01:15) | $44 (standard) | 1 hr 30 min |
| **12:00 – 13:30** | **Lunch – Bryant Park** (e.g., Joe’s Pizza, Le Pain Quotidien) | Outdoor seating with park views. | — | — | 1 hr 30 min |
| **14:00 – 16:30** | **The Metropolitan Museum of Art (The Met)** | • Must‑see: Egyptian Temple, European Paintings, Costume Institute. <br>• Rooftop garden (seasonal) for skyline views. | 10:00 – 17:30 (Fri – 21:00) | $30 (pay‑what‑you‑wish for NY residents) | 2 hr 30 min |
| **17:00 – 18:30** | **Central Park – Walk & Highlights** | • **Bethesda Terrace & Fountain**. <br>• **Bow Bridge** (photo spot). <br>• **The Mall** & **Strawberry Fields**. <br>• Optional bike rental ($25 hr) or Central Park Zoo ($20). | 06:00 – 01:00 | Free (bike/ zoo extra) | 1 hr 30 min |
| **Evening** | **Dinner & Broadway Show** (e.g., Carmine’s, or a pre‑show dinner) | Book a TKTS discount ticket for same‑day shows (up to 50 % off). | — | Show price varies | — |

### Why this route works
- **Iconic Midtown:** Times Square and the Empire State Building set the city’s energy.  
- **Cultural depth:** The Met offers world‑class art in a single, manageable visit if you focus on a few galleries.  
- **Relaxed nature:** Ending with Central Park gives a pleasant contrast to the bustling streets and a perfect spot for sunset photos.  
- **Logistics:** All venues are within a 1‑2 mile radius; a single subway ride (N/Q/R/W to 5th Ave/59th St) or a short taxi can bridge the Met‑to‑Park segment.

---

## 🚇 QUICK TRANSPORT GUIDE  

| Segment | Recommended Subway | Approx. Travel Time |
|---------|-------------------|---------------------|
| Statue → One World | **1** (South Ferry) → walk 5 min | 10 min |
| One World → Brooklyn Bridge | Walk 12 min (south along Fulton St) | – |
| Brooklyn Bridge → DUMBO | Walk across bridge, then 5 min | – |
| DUMBO → Times Square | **A/C** (High St‑Brooklyn Bridge) → **1** (34th St‑Penn) | 25 min |
| Times Square → Empire State | Walk 10 min (or **B/D/F/M** 34th St) | – |
| Empire State → Met | **4** (59th St‑Columbus) → walk 5 min | 10 min |
| Met → Central Park (west side) | Walk across the park (≈15 min) | – |

A **7‑day Unlimited MetroCard** ($33) is the most cost‑effective if you’ll be hopping between sites multiple times a day.

---

## 🎟️ HOW TO BOOK / GET TICKETS  

| Attraction | Best Way to Secure Entry |
|------------|--------------------------|
| **Statue of Liberty** | Reserve a **Reserve Ticket** (pedestal) on the official Statue Cruises site; you’ll receive a QR code for the ferry. |
| **One World Observatory** | Buy tickets online (choose a specific entry time) and consider the “skip‑the‑line” option. |
| **Empire State Building** | Purchase an **Express Pass** for faster security; you can also add the 102‑floor “Top Deck” upgrade. |
| **The Met** | Tickets are sold on‑site; NY residents can pay‑what‑you‑wish. Consider a **membership** if you plan multiple museum visits. |
| **Broadway Show** | Use the **TKTS** booth at Times Square for same‑day discounts (up to 50 % off) or book in advance via Telecharge/SeatGeek. |
| **Central Park Bike Rental** | Reserve a bike from **Bike Rental Central Park** or **Citi Bike** (hourly rates). |

---

